1
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:13,840
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,980
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,180
=Episode 13=

4
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,660
I pay my respects, Your Highness.

5
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,190
I was expecting some stunning beauty.

6
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:08,740
Turns out she's just a village woman.

7
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:11,390
Consort Shu, that's not quite fair.

8
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,750
His Majesty welcomed her himself.

9
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:15,420
She must be quite special.

10
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,110
Rise.

11
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:32,630
Newcomer, serve Consort Chen tea.

12
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,110
Noble Lady Hui.

13
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:35,470
Hold it carefully.

14
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,220
If you drop it,

15
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:39,550
you'd be disrespecting Consort Chen.

16
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:15,020
(They think)

17
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:17,420
(this will take Wanniang down a peg.)

18
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:19,740
(But how could they know)

19
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:22,580
(Wanniang even endured the agony
of burning coals scorching her throat.)

20
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:25,350
(How could she not endure
a little pain like this?)

21
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:30,990
Your tea, Your Highness.

22
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:40,300
Ruolan.

23
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:52,580
I underestimated you.

24
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,300
A wild weed from the countryside.

25
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,350
Tough as leather.

26
00:02:58,300 --> 00:02:59,110
Present your gift.

27
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:03,580
Qing'er.

28
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,990
Just a bolt of Shu brocade.

29
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,279
Quite a feat for a country woman

30
00:03:14,321 --> 00:03:16,020
to offer something this fine.

31
00:03:19,550 --> 00:03:20,670
The brocade may be ordinary,

32
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,049
but a weaver told me

33
00:03:22,091 --> 00:03:24,670
a rather strange tale.

34
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,700
Perhaps it will amuse Your Highness.

35
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:29,670
Oh?

36
00:03:30,990 --> 00:03:31,990
Let's hear it.

37
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,950
Once, there was a wealthy family.

38
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:37,300
The first wife died young,

39
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:38,620
leaving behind

40
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:40,580
a priceless bolt of Shu brocade.

41
00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:44,460
Her husband was devoted.

42
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,950
So he remarried

43
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:48,180
a woman who looked much like her.

44
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,950
To win her husband's affection,

45
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,670
the woman
wore the old Shu brocade every day.

46
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:57,700
But something was strange.

47
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:01,180
It was as if the Shu brocade
knew its owner.

48
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,510
No matter how she wore it,

49
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:05,670
it never sat right on her.

50
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:08,140
So

51
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:11,070
the woman became obsessed.

52
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:14,300
She dug up the first wife's grave,

53
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:15,860
peeled the skin from her corpse,

54
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:17,550
and used it to line her undergarment.

55
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:39,740
Sure enough, when she wore it again,

56
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,150
the garment

57
00:04:41,470 --> 00:04:44,300
fit as if it were part of her body.

58
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:46,990
Her husband saw her

59
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:48,670
and loved her more than ever.

60
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,500
But later,

61
00:04:51,150 --> 00:04:52,500
the woman's flesh

62
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,260
slowly,

63
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:55,470
bit by bit,

64
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:58,790
fused with the dead woman's skin.

65
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,150
Every night,

66
00:05:02,910 --> 00:05:04,590
she heard the same words:

67
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,790
(Roujia, the Late Empress)
(You wore my skin,)

68
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:10,030
(so you'll go to hell with me.)

69
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:12,590
In the end,

70
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,670
the woman clawed at her face

71
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:16,670
until it was raw.

72
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:19,030
She tried to tear off that skin.

73
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:20,740
Unfortunately,

74
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,380
it had fused to her bones by then.

75
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:26,860
(You can't tear it off.)

76
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,820
Your Highness, I heard that

77
00:05:34,230 --> 00:05:35,649
you once favored

78
00:05:35,691 --> 00:05:37,910
gowns made from Shu brocade.

79
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:40,470
After the late Empress passed away,

80
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:42,689
you began wearing

81
00:05:42,731 --> 00:05:44,910
the green patterned satin she favored.

82
00:05:46,150 --> 00:05:48,740
I hope you don't end up like
that woman in the story,

83
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,030
able to shed your clothes

84
00:05:51,590 --> 00:05:53,380
but unable to shed that skin.

85
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,470
I'll take my leave.

86
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:15,799
(That story was terrifying.)

87
00:06:15,841 --> 00:06:16,420
(It really was.)

88
00:06:23,350 --> 00:06:24,380
That village woman

89
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:25,670
has no sense of propriety.

90
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,230
Yuying.

91
00:06:27,550 --> 00:06:28,550
All of you, leave.

92
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:35,260
I'll take my leave.

93
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:07,490
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

94
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:11,690
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

95
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:14,930
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

96
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,000
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

97
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:20,900
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

98
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:24,890
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

99
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:29,250
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

100
00:07:30,170 --> 00:07:32,500
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

101
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:34,680
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

102
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:37,930
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

103
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:42,080
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

104
00:07:43,670 --> 00:07:47,130
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

105
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,960
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

106
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:54,310
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

107
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:58,900
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

108
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:04,130
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

109
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:12,380
♪The past has faded away♪

110
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:16,480
♪The past has faded away♪
